{
  "_comment": "DOCKING CANDIDATE (collar): the plain industrial port. A gunmetal cell body behind a bolted steel flange, and one smooth steel sleeve running in a proud collar that reaches the -Z cell face. The sleeve is a single near-uniform taper, 0.345 at the root to 0.325 at the mouth, with a real bore: two facing ports nest rather than z-fight, and their surfaces cross on ONE circle at the middle of the overlap, which reads as a seal joint. Every detail that could key one port to another - bolt pads, hazard bands, status strip - sits on the BODY, never on the sleeve, so roll is free and no seam gives the overlap away. The cheap default.",
